  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">3Cycle in Ukraine, Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The 3Cycle modular and circular building system addresses the environmental impact of traditional construction by using engineered timber, significantly reducing carbon emissions. Based on design-for-disassembly principles, the system is easy to assemble, relocatable, and open source&#x2014;with publicly available design and manufacturing standards that enable local partners, such as architects and manufacturers, to design, produce, and further develop it. 3Cycle is a flexible system that combines 3D modules and 2D fa&#xe7;ades, offering architectural versatility and making it suitable for a wide range of building types, including schools, nurseries, medical clinics, residential buildings, and offices.In phase 2 of this SBIR innovation challenge, we focus on small medical clinics &#x2014; so-called Feldsher-Akusher Points (FAPs) &#x2014; to help address the shortage of primary healthcare in rural areas of Ukraine. We will construct a demonstration structure to be displayed at a prominent location in either Lviv or Kyiv as proof of concept. In addition, we will further develop the existing BETA version of the digital 3Cycle platform, which consists of a design configurator that enables architects, clients, and other stakeholders to design projects using the 3Cycle system, including real-time information on pricing, environmental performance (comparable to the Dutch MPG score), and carbon emissions.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
